+## Terminal export identity contract
+
+`export_registry(..., terminal_evidence_ref=...)` keeps its existing argument
+name, but a non-null value is only an expected exact identity. The existing
+Registry current execution authority selects status, terminal evidence and
+result bytes at one frozen canonical cut. A missing expected ref still exports
+a current terminal; a nonterminal run returns `terminal_evidence_ref: null` and
+no final user communication. A non-null expectation for a nonterminal run, or
+any wrong, missing, foreign-run or old-generation ref, is rejected.
+
+Historical terminal rows may coexist with a reopened generation. They neither
+close an open generation nor replace the current generation's selected evidence.
+Active-firing provisional facts remain available only with `include_provisional`;
+terminal authority and its result always require canonical visibility. Missing
+current authority, inconsistent exact identity/closure, or a changed Registry
+head/writer epoch fails closed, leaving the caller's observations unchanged.
+No export starts a writer, resumes a run, invokes a provider or repairs evidence.
+
+The returned terminal ref and final communication's raw evidence come from the
+same verified Registry chain. `capture_diagnostics.terminal_identity` reports the
+current authority ref, status, generation, terminal/result refs, native
+`run_outcome`, head ordinal and writer epoch (`rpnh-ha/current-terminal-identity/v1`).
+The projection revision is `execution-return-registry-reader-v3`; offline
+reprojection provenance uses that same exporter revision.
+`stop_reason` remains the caller's diagnostic and does not establish terminality
+or business success. Existing capture/scoring semantics and published scores
+are unchanged. Offline reprojection checks its saved driver ref by this same
+contract; an outdated sidecar must not be silently substituted into a report.
